{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554011-extended-rolls-for-wonders","id":1554011,"title":"Extended rolls for wonders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-25T11:24:37-07:00","id":1554011,"title":"Extended rolls for wonders","content":"Since Artifacts and Fetishes only need 1 success for activation, I guess a better title would be &quot;extended rolls for Talismans&quot; <br /> I'm using Forged by Dragon's Fire system for wonders, but if there is something about that in M20 (or any other edition) I'd like to know too.<br /> <br /> So, in FbDF page 53 we have this Talisman called Mater Transmission Portal (Arete 4, Quintessence 5). It's system works like that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System: To locate a specific person or place using the portal, the user must first adjust the device by making an Intelligence + Technology ro ll with a difficulty of 5 to see a location, and a difficulty of 7 to<br /> actually open a portal. After making this roll, the user<br /> rolls the Device's Arete of 4, subtracting one from the<br /> difficulty for every success on the Intelligence + Tech-<br /> nology rpoll (to a maximum of -3). Use the Correspondence Ranges chart to determine the num-<br /> ber of successes the user must obtain. Both uses of the Device remain active for one full scene.<br /> If the user rolls well enough to open a portal. she<br /> can leave the portal closed for a time and simply observe the location, without needing to make a second roll to open the portal later in the scene. (\u2026) </div> </div> </div> So, using abilities enhancing magick is a thing for wonders (which I didn't knew) and a lot of this books Talisman use it. Now, the question is: can extended Arete rolls be used as well? <br /> <br /> If not, then that means that the wonder in question isn't able to open a portal to anywhere in the world since the correspondence table requires 6+ successes for that? Moreso, the limit is a portal to somewhere you have visited before, as this one requires 4 successes, and that's considering you can get all 4 Arete successes. Most likely you will only be able to open a portal to a very familiar place.<br /> <br /> This seems to be quite limiting and maybe wonders shouls have extended rolls as well? Any reason for why not? Is there any raw about that?<br /> <br /> If not, how doea your table handle this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T12:39:03-07:00","id":1554015,"title":"","content":"IIRC the RAW is that Wonders don't do Extended Arete Rolls, period. This is a benefit for true Mages alone.<br /> <br /> That said, the game also has a long tradition of not following its own rules when making stuff, and Wonders are no exception, so...<br /> <br /> Myself, I usually go for a case by case approach with Wonders. I see four alternative approaches here, none of them RAW because RAW simply won't work well for this.<br /> <br /> 1- Count successes above 3 in the Ability roll as extra success in the Arete roll, just to buff this up a bit;<br /> <br /> 2- Do the Extended Action thing, maybe with custom roll duration for the Wonder;<br /> <br /> 3- Reduce the number of successes needed so you can get all the options you want within the 4 possible successes;<br /> <br /> 4- Give it a set effect within the options in the table and run it with a single success, find out any other benefit you want for extra successes, this always makes a lot of sense for Wonders.<br /> <br /> You can also simply run it RAW and call it a day. An item that can open portals within the ranges of the table is already good within the scope of what a Wonder does. Wonders aren't meant to be very versatile, they're just a cheap alternative to actually having the Spheres to do the stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T06:19:02-07:00","id":1554021,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, thank you for your answer. While your options are good, I'd rather use extended rolls or your 5th option (no extended roll and wonders are limited in this way). I think the first option would make more sense, though. I'm only thinking if that would be a game breaker\u2026<br /> <br /> Now, in raw wonders can't use extended Arete rolls. Do you have some reference? I'm only asking this because I could swear that you could not use &quot;ability enhancing magick&quot; with wonders, but here they are. To me, that makes as much sense as extended rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T07:14:55-07:00","id":1554022,"title":"","content":"Well M20 doesn't say anything one way or the other about extended rolls for wonders, at least not that I can find, and the section on extended rolls and rituals doesn't exclude wonders. Within the fiction it is easy to see someone struggling with such a device and spending a few turns trying to get a lock on with the device. So I'd say it is reasonable to use extended rolls.<br /> <br /> Also, in many cases it would make more sense for the user to first use the device to see the location or place. That scouting might take 6+ successes if the user doesn't know what he's looking for, but more likely takes 5 successes if he is thinking of a specific place and can describe it. That arguably reduces the Correspondence range of the target to line of site (1) for a subsequent teleportation use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T07:44:50-07:00","id":1554023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554011-extended-rolls-for-wonders?p=1554022#post1554022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well M20 doesn't say anything one way or the other about extended rolls for wonders, at least not that I can find, and the section on extended rolls and rituals doesn't exclude wonders. Within the fiction it is easy to see someone struggling with such a device and spending a few turns trying to get a lock on with the device. So I'd say it is reasonable to use extended rolls.<br /> <br /> Also, in many cases it would make more sense for the user to first use the device to see the location or place. That scouting might take 6+ successes if the user doesn't know what he's looking for, but more likely takes 5 successes if he is thinking of a specific place and can describe it. That arguably reduces the Correspondence range of the target to line of site (1) for a subsequent teleportation use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great points. Yeah, I never seen anything regarding wonders Arete rolls, but personally, I'd think it wasn't a thing. But after seeing practically every Talisman in FbDF using the abilities enhancing magick rule (which is pretty similar to extended rolls), I have changed my mind.<br /> <br /> Now, having said that, how would such rule work? I mean, what are the limits of the rolls? I'd say, since the raw limit is WP+Arete, maybe having the Talisman's arete as a limit (so in the example, 4 rolls). Or maybe the mage's WP+wonder Arete? What you think?<br /> <br /> Also, would it be like a ritual (no increase in diff) or like the &quot;picking up&quot; rule (+1 diff for each roll)? Maybe depending if the mage is doing the stuff quickly or calmly, just like a real Arete roll?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T08:09:57-07:00","id":1554024,"title":"","content":"If I was asked at the table and had to make a quick decision, I'd say it is WP of the user, though maybe someone who has Arete could also add the Arete of the device. I'd also use standard ritual rules, which only increase in difficulty if there's a failed roll.<br /> <br /> If someone was unpracticed with the device and under stress it would make narrative sense that they have to use &quot;picking up&quot; rule because they are not prepared to use it properly, but only for that situation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-28T15:21:06-07:00","id":1554040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554011-extended-rolls-for-wonders?p=1554022#post1554022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well M20 doesn't say anything one way or the other about extended rolls for wonders, at least not that I can find, and the section on extended rolls and rituals doesn't exclude wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, in fact, an example in M20 of a Device using extended rolls. The Sleepteacher in Technocracy Reloaded p185 uses extended rolls. The description specifically states that <i>&quot;The effect is then performed as a ritual (see Mage 20 pp. 538-540) with each period of six or more hours under the influence of the Sleepteacher permitting one roll.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Perhaps adapting these mechanics to the Matter Transmission Portal would make it slower to use, but give it a wider range ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26426,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","user":"Trianoma4Evah","date":". 09-28-2025, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T10:01:28-07:00","id":1554060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554011-extended-rolls-for-wonders?p=1554040#post1554040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is, in fact, an example in M20 of a Device using extended rolls. The Sleepteacher in Technocracy Reloaded p185 uses extended rolls. The description specifically states that <i>&quot;The effect is then performed as a ritual (see Mage 20 pp. 538-540) with each period of six or more hours under the influence of the Sleepteacher permitting one roll.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Perhaps adapting these mechanics to the Matter Transmission Portal would make it slower to use, but give it a wider range ?</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> Thank you very much for your answer! This means extended rolls for wonders are indeed raw.<br /> <br /> Yes, I believe that what tells how long it takes for the ritual is how the wonder itself works. The sleepteacher is used during long periods of sleep, so it makes sense for taking 6h for a roll.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Matter Transmission Portal, it work by adjusting the device, which I believe could take just a few minutes per roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T10:49:07-07:00","id":1554084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554011-extended-rolls-for-wonders?p=1554060#post1554060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I believe that what tells how long it takes for the ritual is how the wonder itself works. The sleepteacher is used during long periods of sleep, so it makes sense for taking 6h for a roll.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Matter Transmission Portal, it work by adjusting the device, which I believe could take just a few minutes per roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might end up with an overpowered device with that approach, since it will outperform a mage by accumulating a considerable amount of successes much faster than a mage could.<br /> <br /> You may want to apply the durations from the &quot;Optional Rule: Rite, Ceremony, and Great Work&quot; (M20 p541), with the device performing better if you take your time instead of rushing things. (For 2 rolls, you can get it ready in minutes, for up to 5 rolls, ready in hours, for up to willpower+arete rolls, 6 hours per roll)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T12:41:12-07:00","id":1554087,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> <br /> And for the purpose of a portal, this mechanic it's still going to take &quot;just&quot; minutes, probably, unless it's being used in a very outlandish way. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> pointed out, scanning the location first seems like the wise move, and it's an easy enough Efffect that it's reasonable to get it on two checks of Arete 4. Then teleporting it's a <i>different </i>Effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-01-2025, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T19:30:26-07:00","id":1554095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554011-extended-rolls-for-wonders?p=1554084#post1554084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might end up with an overpowered device with that approach, since it will outperform a mage by accumulating a considerable amount of successes much faster than a mage could.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a problem, actually.<br /> <br /> However effective the Wonder is at doing it's thing, it still does only one thing, and in only one way. Especially if you use the rules for Creative Thaumaturgy, a Mage can use the extra successes for a lot of other purposes in devising this portal even if you keep to the specific effect of making a portal. The Wonder just opens it or not and that's it.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think the Wonder having a specific advantage isn't a problem, and being able to work faster (if still not combat-fast) is a pretty good option. How frequently will this <i>for real</i> affect the game other than by making an item meant to be used to be actually feasible to use?<br /> <br /> Even because you should have a reason for a Mage with access to the same Magic of the Wonder to still see utility in having the Wonder. Characters that chose to have a Wonder for Magic they can do should still get something out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T05:48:53-07:00","id":1554100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even because you should have a reason for a Mage with access to the same Magic of the Wonder to still see utility in having the Wonder. Characters that chose to have a Wonder for Magic they can do should still get something out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since he's using FbDF and it's a Talisman, I would suggest that while the device requires an action to do the Skill checks, it<i> wouldn't</i> require an action to roll Arete. So, it can ritual on it's own. And so the portal - or the whatever -can be left &quot;loading&quot; on it's own while your mage goes about their other stuff.<br /> <br /> That's a pretty powerful advantage backed on the rules of FbDF. And also I think it could be cool for stories. Like, you can have a mad scientist activating a &quot;doomsday device&quot; - or otherwise dangerous stuff (heat ray to melt the pole, death ray to nuke the city, open a portal to hell, etc ... that RAW would be pretty hard to do in any serious capacity under one Arete roll, at least w/o Archspheres), and the party needing to <i>both </i>defeat th scientist and deal with the device, to break or de-activate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-02-2025, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T09:14:28-07:00","id":1554104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554011-extended-rolls-for-wonders?p=1554084#post1554084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You might end up with an overpowered device with that approach, since it will outperform a mage by accumulating a considerable amount of successes much faster than a mage could.<br /> <br /> You may want to apply the durations from the &quot;Optional Rule: Rite, Ceremony, and Great Work&quot; (M20 p541), with the device performing better if you take your time instead of rushing things. (For 2 rolls, you can get it ready in minutes, for up to 5 rolls, ready in hours, for up to willpower+arete rolls, 6 hours per roll)</div> </div> </div> </div> That's an option, yeah, but as monteparnas, I don't think that would be a problem, especially for that wonder, where 6 successes is all you need. Still, even for other wonders, I don't see that as an issue, because, again as posted, the wonder does one (or just a few) single effects. It will *never* be better than having a Sphere.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding the optional rule, I like to have raw guides but it doesn't fit quite well in my mind.<br /> <br /> \u2264 5 successes: 5 minutes<br /> 6 to 10 successes: 1 hour per roll<br /> &gt; 10 successes: 5 hours per roll<br /> <br /> I find it hard most instruments using 5+ hours. Like, your mage is using eye contact. Would you stare at something for 10 hours? Doesn't seem realistic. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> Im not sure the skill check is required, it seems to be just a way to reduce difficulty as in &quot;abilities enhance magick&quot;. In fbdf, a lot (almost all) of the Talismans have skill checks, idk how that would work with that whole Talismans activating themselves thing\u2026<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T12:04:30-07:00","id":1554107,"title":"","content":"Well, most Talismans don't have their own skills. Yet FbDF makes a point in saying that could happen. If the roll it's just to lower diffs then I would say they just don't get that bonus on that case. But if it's a roll to activate the Talisman, however, that's an issue.<br /> <br /> I think I would use the skills of their creator in that case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it hard most instruments using 5+ hours. Like, your mage is using eye contact. Would you stare at something for 10 hours? Doesn't seem realistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not adamantly against changing the rules if it makes more sense, and for the limited case of Artifacts that could be a feasible &quot;bonus&quot;, altorough I don't think it's all that necessary.<br /> <br /> BUT ... in this case I think it's just better to make form fit fuction and rule that if it doesn't make sense for your Mage to be staring 10 hours, then you just can't do magick that way. Use another Instrument.<br /> <br /> Like, an altar isn't as portable as &quot;eye contact&quot;, but it's easy enough to justify a 5 hours ceremony arround it. Instruments having pros and cons it's already a thing. Some instruments are mechanically better than others.<br /> <br /> But I think allowing some Instruments (like &quot;eye contact&quot;) the immensely powerful bonus of just casting everything a lot faster WOULD increase the problem of some Instruments just being better than others by lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-02-2025, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T08:04:23-07:00","id":1554143,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> What point that fbdf makes that you are talking about? And you mean that eye contact woulndt be able to do great works? Or even, *any* instrument that &quot;can't&quot; be used for like 5+ hours shouldn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}